.TH FAST2BAN-CLIENT "1" "October 2026" "Fast2Ban v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fast2ban-client \- configure and control the Fast2Ban server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fast2ban-client
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfast2ban-client\fR communicates with \fBfast2ban-server\fR over a Unix domain socket
to configure, query, start, stop, reload, and unban IP addresses across jails.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR <DIR>
Configuration directory (default: \fI/etc/fail2ban\fR).
.TP
\fB\-s\fR <FILE>
Socket path to connect to.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR <FILE>
PID file path.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR
Dump configuration command stream to stdout for debugging.
.TP
\fB\-\-dp\fR
Dump configuration in human-readable formatted representation.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR
Test configuration parsing without connecting to a server.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR
Decrease verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version.
.TP
\fB\-\-str2sec\fR <STRING>
Convert time duration string (e.g., \fI1d\fR, \fI2h\fR, \fI30m\fR) to seconds.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBstart\fR
Start server if not running and stream active configuration.
.TP
\fBstop\fR [\fIJAIL\fR]
Stop server or specified jail.
.TP
\fBrestart\fR [\fIJAIL\fR]
Restart server or specified jail.
.TP
\fBreload\fR [\fI\-\-restart\fR] [\fI\-\-unban\fR] [\fI\-\-if\-exists\fR] [\fIJAIL\fR]
Reload configuration without dropping active bans.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR [\fI\-\-all\fR | \fIJAIL\fR]
Display overview or detailed failure and ban statistics for a jail.
.TP
\fBunban\fR \fIIP\fR... | \fI\-\-all\fR
Unban specified IP address(es) across all jails.
.TP
\fBbanned\fR [\fIIP\fR...]
Check if IP address(es) are banned across jails.
.TP
\fBflushlogs\fR
Flush and reopen log files (for logrotate integration).
.TP
\fBset\fR \fIJAIL\fR \fIOPTION\fR \fIVALUE\fR...
Set jail parameters at runtime (\fImaxretry\fR, \fIfindtime\fR, \fIbantime\fR, \fIbanip\fR, \fIunbanip\fR).
.TP
\fBget\fR \fIJAIL\fR \fIOPTION\fR
Query runtime parameters and banned lists.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
fast2ban-server(1), fast2ban-regex(1), jail.conf(5)
